#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:106
msgid "Principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:107
msgid ""
"**Compression as identity**: Geist Sans at display sizes uses -2.4px to "
"-2.88px letter-spacing — the most aggressive negative tracking of any "
"major design system. This creates text that feels _minified_, like code "
"optimized for production. The tracking progressively relaxes as size "
"decreases: -1.28px at 32px, -0.96px at 24px, -0.32px at 16px, and normal "
"at 14px."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:108
msgid ""
"**Ligatures everywhere**: Every Geist text element enables OpenType "
"`\"liga\"`. Ligatures aren't decorative — they're structural, creating "
"tighter, more efficient glyph combinations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:109
msgid ""
"**Three weights, strict roles**: 400 (body/reading), 500 "
"(UI/interactive), 600 (headings/emphasis). No bold (700) except for tiny "
"micro-badges. This narrow weight range creates hierarchy through size and"
" tracking, not weight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:110
msgid ""
"**Mono for identity**: Geist Mono in uppercase with `\"tnum\"` or "
"`\"liga\"` serves as the \"developer console\" voice — compact technical "
"labels that connect the marketing site to the product."
msgstr ""

