#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:235
msgid ""
"**Shadow Philosophy**: Vercel has arguably the most sophisticated shadow "
"system in modern web design. Rather than using shadows for elevation in "
"the traditional Material Design sense, Vercel uses multi-value shadow "
"stacks where each layer has a distinct architectural purpose: one creates"
" the \"border\" (0px spread, 1px), another adds ambient softness (2px "
"blur), another handles depth at distance (8px blur with negative spread),"
" and an inner ring (`#fafafa`) creates the subtle highlight that makes "
"the card \"glow\" from within. This layered approach means cards feel "
"built, not floating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:237
msgid "Decorative Depth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:238
msgid ""
"Hero gradient: soft, pastel multi-color gradient wash behind hero content"
" (barely visible, atmospheric)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:239
msgid ""
"Section borders: `1px solid #171717` (full dark line) between major "
"sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:240
msgid ""
"No background color variation — depth comes entirely from shadow layering"
" and border contrast"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:242
msgid "7. Do's and Don'ts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:244
msgid "Do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:245
msgid ""
"Use Geist Sans with aggressive negative letter-spacing at display sizes "
"(-2.4px to -2.88px at 48px)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:246
msgid ""
"Use shadow-as-border (`0px 0px 0px 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.08)`) instead of "
"traditional CSS borders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:247
msgid ""
"Enable `\"liga\"` on all Geist text — ligatures are structural, not "
"optional"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:248
msgid "Use the three-weight system: 400 (body), 500 (UI), 600 (headings)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:249
msgid ""
"Apply workflow accent colors (Red/Pink/Blue) only in their workflow "
"context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:250
msgid ""
"Use multi-layer shadow stacks for cards (border + elevation + ambient + "
"inner highlight)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:251
msgid ""
"Keep the color palette achromatic — grays from `#171717` to `#ffffff` are"
" the system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:252
msgid ""
"Use `#171717` instead of `#000000` for primary text — the micro-warmth "
"matters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:254
msgid "Don't"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:255
msgid ""
"Don't use positive letter-spacing on Geist Sans — it's always negative or"
" zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:256
msgid ""
"Don't use weight 700 (bold) on body text — 600 is the maximum, used only "
"for headings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:257
msgid ""
"Don't use traditional CSS `border` on cards — use the shadow-border "
"technique"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:258
msgid "Don't introduce warm colors (oranges, yellows, greens) into the UI chrome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:259
msgid ""
"Don't apply the workflow accent colors (Ship Red, Preview Pink, Develop "
"Blue) decoratively"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:260
msgid ""
"Don't use heavy shadows (> 0.1 opacity) — the shadow system is whisper-"
"level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:261
msgid "Don't increase body text letter-spacing — Geist is designed to run tight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:262
msgid ""
"Don't use pill radius (9999px) on primary action buttons — pills are for "
"badges/tags only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_vercel.md:263
msgid ""
"Don't skip the inner `#fafafa` ring in card shadows — it's the glow that "
"makes the system work"
msgstr ""

